  <static seed="622" source="Library/Michigan/Chap16Sec5/Q11.pg">
    <statement><p>Evaluate, in spherical coordinates, the triple integral of
<m>f(\rho,\theta,\phi) = \sin\phi</m>, over the region
<m>0 \le \theta \le 2\pi</m>,
<m>0 \le \phi \le \pi/3</m>,
<m>3 \le \rho \le 4</m>.</p>
<p>integral = <fillin characters="35" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\frac{\pi }{6}\mathopen{}\left(4^{3}-3^{3}\right)\mathopen{}\left(\frac{2\pi }{3}-\sin\mathopen{}\left(\frac{2\pi }{3}\right)\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><me>\int_W f\,dV
   = \int_0^{2\pi} \int_{0}^{\pi/3} \int_{3}^{4}
	(\sin\phi)\rho^2 \sin \phi\,d\rho\,d\phi\,d\theta
   = \int_0^{2\pi} \int_{0}^{\pi/3}
	(\sin^2\phi)(\frac13)(\rho^3)\bigg|_{\rho=3}^{\rho=4}
	\,d\phi\,d\theta</me>
<me>= \frac{37}{3} \int_0^{2\pi} \int_{0}^{\pi/3} \frac12(1 - \cos2\phi)\, d\phi\,d\theta
   = \frac{37}{3} \int_0^{2\pi} \frac12(\phi - \frac12\sin2\phi)\bigg|_{\phi=0}^{\phi=\pi/3}\,d\theta</me>
<me>= \frac{37}{6} (\frac{\pi}3 - \sin(\frac{2\pi}3)) \int_0^{2\pi}\frac12\,d\theta = \frac{37}{6} (\frac{\pi}3 - \sin(\frac{2\pi}3)) \pi.</me>



</solution>
